We currently have a vacancy for a Performance/Resilience Test Engineer fluent in English, to offer his/her services as an expert remotely (within EU). In the context of the first assignment, the successful candidate will be integrated in the Development team of the company that will closely cooperate with a major client’s IT team. Tasks:
Create the non-functional test plan and update the test plan for review to manager/leader;
Plan, prepare execute and analyse the non-functional testing activities as required;
Develop a strategy for end-to-end non-functional testing of the solution;
Develop the performance test script using the tools available for all the identified performance and resilience testing scenarios; involve in preparation of performance test data;
Execute the various non-functional tests including resilience, recovery, load test, stress test, endurance test, capacity test;
Analyse the resource usage during test execution to verify the performance of the applications and identify bottleneck problem in the application;
Review test results captured during test execution, support the identification of non-functional issues and make recommendations;
Enable other QA engineers and developers in running non-functional tests;
Provide technical assistance to improve system performance, capacity, reliability and scalability;
Develop standards and best practices for writing robust, maintainable, and performant load testing scripts;
Evaluate system performances and stability and recommend improvements.

University degree in IT combined with relevant professional experience of at least 6 years in non-functional testing and associated tooling;
Expertise in Test Planning, Test Estimation, Test Strategy, Workload Design, Test Cases Design, Test Platform Setup, Test Data Setup and Defect Management;
Good Hands-on knowledge on performance test tool JMeter or Gatling;
Capacity in writing documents;
Ability to present findings and recommendations to team members, management and customers;
Experience in agile software development and testing methodologies;
Experience using Chaos/Kraken for resilience testing will be considered a plus;
Hands on Java experience from automation point of view will be considered a plus;
Experience in complex setups including several integrated systems will be considered a plus;
Experience in micro-services based private cloud hosted solution will be considered a plus;
Excellent command of the English language.
Benefits If you are seeking a career in an exciting and dynamic company, where you will offer your services as part of a team of a major European Institution, operating in an international, multilingual and multicultural environment where you can expect real chances to make a difference, please send us your detailed CV in English, quoting reference: (ST/PRTER/08/2026).

We offer a competitive remuneration (either on contract basis or remuneration with full benefits package), based on qualifications and experience. All applications will be treated as confidential.

You may also consider all our other open vacancies by visiting the career section of our web site (www.eurodyn.com) and follow us on Twitter (@EURODYN_Careers) and LinkedIn.

EUROPEAN DYNAMICS ( ) is a leading Software, Information and Communication Technologies company, operating internationally (Athens, Brussels, Luxembourg, Copenhagen, Stockholm, London, Nicosia, Hong-Kong, Valetta, etc). The company employs over 1000 engineers, IT experts and consultants (around 3% PhD, 36% MSc and 53% BSc or equivalent).

We design and develop software applications using state-of-the-art technology. The group generates annual revenues in the range of EURO 40 million, with an EBITDA in the range of 20%. The value of our contract portfolio exceeds EURO 300 million.

EUROPEAN DYNAMICS is a renowned supplier of IT services to government institutions, multinational corporations, public administrations and multinational companies, research and academic institutes.

As part of our dedication to the diversity of our workforce, we are committed to Equal Employment Opportunity without regard for race, color, national origin, ethnicity, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, or religion EUROPEAN DYNAMICS (ED) adheres to the General Data Protection Regulation principles by applying its Privacy Policy as published in www.eurodyn.com/privacy.

By submitting an application to this position and by sharing your personal data with ED, you acknowledge and accept its Policy and authorize ED to process your personal data for the purposes of the company's recruitment opportunities, in line to the Policy. Originally posted on Himalayas

Testing games manually (black box testing);
Identify and track project issues;
Pay attention to user experience, gameplay mechanics, graphics, and audio elements to ensure a seamless gaming experience;
Participate in the planning and execution of QA activities throughout all phases of the sprint lifecycle;
Reviewing and analyzing game design documents and functional specifications;
Creating test documentation (test plans, traceability matrix, test cases, checklists, test reports);
Designing, implementing, and maintaining automated testing suites using tools like Playwright;
Facilitating smooth releases and collaboration with a team;
Provide feedback and suggestions to improve quality and game experience.

You like to troubleshoot technical problems and try to get to the root of why weird error messages come up. You are proactive and used to taking ownership and responsibility. You are not afraid of information analysis. You see yourself as a good team player.
Good written and verbal communications skills in English - ability to describe identified issues in a clear and concise manner;
At least 5 years of relevant experience in software testing (gamedev is a strong plus);
A methodical, scientific and analytical mindset;
Knowledgeable about SDLC and STLC;
Expert in Test Design techniques and their applicability on practice;
Strong Knowledge about Testing types and levels and their applicability;
Experience with Agile development methodologies, processes and tools;
Experience with multiple platforms (mobile, desktop, web, social platforms);
Experience with Jira or similar software;
Experience with TestRail or similar software;

Certification like ISTQB;
Test automation experience: ability to write, review, and debug end-to-end automated tests;
Proficiency with at least one modern programming language with a preference for JavaScript/TypeScript;
Familiarity with Playwright/Cypress/WebdriverIO or another web test automation tool;
Experience with version control and CI integration (Jenkins/GitHub/GitLab).

An international team of 50+ professionals from almost 20 different countries;
Work closely with some of the biggest (upcoming) game platforms in the world on high-quality casual games that are played by millions of gamers;
Competitive remuneration;
A flexible remote working environment;
A very open, informal and international company culture where everyone can make a difference.
